1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,478
AI agents can change code in seconds. But

2
00:00:03,478 --> 00:00:06,707
a real project is more than code: it

3
00:00:06,707 --> 00:00:09,128
carries intent, rules, and promises. When

4
00:00:09,128 --> 00:00:10,742
those disappear between tasks,

5
00:00:10,742 --> 00:00:11,953
speed becomes drift.

6
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,078
You tell Codex what you want. Instead of

7
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:18,552
scanning the whole project from scratch on

8
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:21,026
every task, Codex consults Sema for the

9
00:00:21,026 --> 00:00:23,501
context that matters, then works from a

10
00:00:23,501 --> 00:00:24,561
precise semantic map.

11
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:32,479
On first contact, the real bootstrap runs

12
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:36,169
in a small payments project with no Sema

13
00:00:36,169 --> 00:00:39,859
and no AGENTS.md. It checks the local CLI,

14
00:00:39,859 --> 00:00:42,626
creates the first living contract, and

15
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:44,932
generates its AGENTS.md, the permanent

16
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:46,316
handshake future Codex

17
00:00:46,316 --> 00:00:47,700
tasks read automatically.

18
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:51,071
The living contract preserves your intent,

19
00:00:51,071 --> 00:00:53,422
rules, guarantees, and semantic links,

20
00:00:53,422 --> 00:00:56,243
leading Codex directly to the relevant

21
00:00:56,243 --> 00:00:59,065
code. Codex implements the request. Sema

22
00:00:59,065 --> 00:01:00,945
then verifies that implementation

23
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,356
against the contract.

24
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:05,724
The task is concrete: complete a payment

25
00:01:05,724 --> 00:01:07,492
approval rename from approvePayment to

26
00:01:07,492 --> 00:01:09,259
confirmPayment without losing the receipt

27
00:01:09,259 --> 00:01:11,380
guarantee. A partial rename already exists

28
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:13,855
in the code, while the semantic contract

29
00:01:13,855 --> 00:01:16,682
still points to the old symbol. It is

30
00:01:16,682 --> 00:01:18,803
a quiet mismatch that could poison

31
00:01:18,803 --> 00:01:19,864
the next change.

32
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:27,901
Before editing, Codex asks Sema for

33
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:29,668
context, required documentation, and

34
00:01:29,668 --> 00:01:32,319
drift. Sema resolves the contract against

35
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:34,970
the implementation and stops the change:

36
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:38,062
the old approvePayment link is broken. The

37
00:01:38,062 --> 00:01:41,155
result names the contract, the symbol, and

38
00:01:41,155 --> 00:01:44,248
the affected files. No guesswork, and no

39
00:01:44,248 --> 00:01:45,573
fake green check.

40
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:51,516
Codex inspects the applicable dot-sema

41
00:01:51,516 --> 00:01:54,236
contract, maps the impact, then updates

42
00:01:54,236 --> 00:01:56,502
the contract and implementation together.

43
00:01:56,502 --> 00:01:58,769
The business promise remains explicit:

44
00:01:58,769 --> 00:02:01,488
every approved payment returns a receipt

45
00:02:01,488 --> 00:02:04,208
ID. Validation passes, the symbol link

46
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:06,928
resolves, tests pass, and drift returns

47
00:02:06,928 --> 00:02:10,101
green. Only then does Sema close the

48
00:02:10,101 --> 00:02:12,367
change with its required documentation

49
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:13,727
recorded as evidence.

50
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:18,585
I use Sema entirely through Codex. Build

51
00:02:18,585 --> 00:02:21,921
Week made me stop building a separate

52
00:02:21,921 --> 00:02:24,779
OpenCode-based IDE and stop spreading Sema

53
00:02:24,779 --> 00:02:27,162
across every assistant. With GPT-5.6

54
00:02:27,162 --> 00:02:30,974
through Codex, I made the CLI the engine,

55
00:02:30,974 --> 00:02:33,832
AGENTS.md the handshake, and the plugin

56
00:02:33,832 --> 00:02:36,215
first contact—then verified the public

57
00:02:36,215 --> 00:02:39,074
package. Sema governs its own development.

58
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:44,013
Software is the proving ground, not the

59
00:02:44,013 --> 00:02:46,701
boundary. The same chain—intent, context,

60
00:02:46,701 --> 00:02:48,852
contract, impact, execution, evidence—can

61
00:02:48,852 --> 00:02:52,078
govern any structured work performed by

62
00:02:52,078 --> 00:02:55,303
agents. Sema: from human intent to

63
00:02:55,303 --> 00:02:56,916
verified AI execution.

